From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 13:39:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] block: partitions: efi: bound partition name length for OF lookup

KASAN reports a slab-out-of-bounds read in find_partition_of_node()
(via mmc_rescan) when scanning GPT entries for an OF partition match.

The size argument of utf16_le_to_7bit() is the number of UTF-16LE
symbols to read from @in, not the capacity of @out.  volname is
char[64], so this asks for 63 symbols (126 bytes), but
gpt_entry::partition_name is

	__le16 partition_name[72/sizeof(__le16)];	/* block/partitions/efi.h */

i.e. 36 symbols / 72 bytes.  Every call therefore reads 27 __le16 past
the end of the name field.  For all but the last partition entry the
surplus lands inside the following gpt_entry and merely corrupts
volname; for the last entry it runs off the end of the array
alloc_read_gpt_entries() allocated.

Bound the symbol count by the size of partition_name as well.

Signed-off-by: Sean McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>
---
 block/partitions/efi.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/block/partitions/efi.c b/block/partitions/efi.c
index ac2c7d3c4993..62dcb6b233b6 100644
--- a/block/partitions/efi.c
+++ b/block/partitions/efi.c
@@ -700,13 +700,15 @@ static struct device_node *find_partition_of_node(struct device_node *partitions
 {
 	char volname[64], partuuid[UUID_STRING_LEN + 1];
 	const char *uuid, *name;
+	unsigned int label_max;
 
 	if (!partitions_np ||
 	    !of_device_is_compatible(partitions_np, "gpt-partitions"))
 		return NULL;
 
 	efi_guid_to_str(&ptes->unique_partition_guid, partuuid);
-	utf16_le_to_7bit(ptes->partition_name, ARRAY_SIZE(volname) - 1, volname);
+	label_max = min(ARRAY_SIZE(volname) - 1, ARRAY_SIZE(ptes->partition_name));
+	utf16_le_to_7bit(ptes->partition_name, label_max, volname);
 
 	for_each_available_child_of_node_scoped(partitions_np, np) {
 		if (!of_property_read_string(np, "uuid", &uuid) &&
